//! Wave 7c, frontier W (record uo-bindings.md "Wave 7c — W"): the Rust layout against Microsoft Word's own PDFs.
//!
//! A minimal port of the frozen TS `test/oracle-compare.ts` (`engineLines` + `compareLines`) over the oracle groups this
//! frontier added under `tests/oracle_w7c/<group>` (generated by `write/tools/layout-oracle`, cases `cases/<group>.mjs`,
//! `run.mjs <group> --fixdir`; the `.word.json` are the lines Word 16 pt-BR wrote in its PDF of each `.docx`). The groups
//! use the open fonts only (Liberation Sans, Carlito), so the test runs anywhere the repository's fonts are.
//!
//! Each case is laid out twice: with the default options (Word's rules: every case must equal Word — pages, line texts in
//! order, the page of each line, baseline ±0.3 pt, x where the group measures it) and with `LayoutOptions::ts_strict()`
//! (the frozen TS's rules): the cases where the TS differs from Word are listed per group (`ts_diverges`), so this test
//! also documents each divergence.
//!
//!   cargo test -j 3 --release -p uo-docx-layout --test word_w7c -- --test-threads=3
//!   UO_W7C_VERBOSE=1: one line per case

#![cfg(not(target_family = "wasm"))] // the system font index and the files of the oracle groups
#![allow(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used, clippy::panic, clippy::indexing_slicing)] // test harness

